.TH DEVID-ENROLL 1 "October 2026" "vtpm-mds" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
devid-enroll \- enroll or renew a guest LDevID via vtpm-mds
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B devid-enroll
.RB [ \-tpm
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-mds
.IR url ]
.RB [ \-out
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-cn
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-spire-data
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Guest helper that authenticates to
.B vtpm-mds
with MAC inventory identity and the TPM EK certificate, then writes SPIRE
.B tpm_devid
materials (PEM + TPM2B blobs).
.PP
On each run it renews when the certificate is missing, unreadable, expired, or
in the last third of its validity, and also when the materials do not fit:
the certificate's subject
.B CN
is not this guest's VM ID, a DevID blob is missing or empty, the
certificate's public key is not the key in
.IR devid.pub.blob ,
or the blobs do not load in this TPM under the SPIRE H-1 storage parent, as
after a clone that got a new vTPM or a replaced vTPM. Otherwise it exits
successfully without calling enroll. Each renewal logs its reason:
.IR "no certificate" ,
.IR "unreadable certificate" ,
.IR due ,
.IR "certificate is for another VM" ,
.IR "missing blob" ,
.I "certificate does not match key"
or
.IR "key does not load in this TPM" .
.PP
The VM ID is
.I /latest/meta-data/instance-id
from the service named by
.BR \-mds ,
without its
.B i-
prefix, read with an IMDSv2 session token. Every run that finds a readable
certificate reads it, also when nothing is due; a first enrollment does not.
It is tried three times over about ten seconds. When it still cannot be read,
or does not start with
.BR i- ,
the run exits non-zero, makes no enroll request and changes no file. The
host serves
.I instance-id
only with
.B enable_ec2_compat
on; with it off, every run with a certificate fails although enrollment
itself would work.
.PP
Every run also derives the storage parent and loads the DevID key, a few
seconds of TPM work on a vTPM. When the blobs load, a renewal reuses that
key; when they do not decode or the TPM refuses them for integrity, binding
or sensitive-area reasons, it creates a new key, as a first enrollment does.
Any other TPM error, including a warning such as
.B TPM_RC_RETRY
or
.BR TPM_RC_OBJECT_MEMORY ,
fails the run with no enroll request and the files unchanged, so a
transient fault never discards a working key; the next run tries again.
.PP
When the certificate PEM bytes change and
.B \-spire-data
is set, the helper removes the SPIRE agent SVID cache file
.I agent-data.json
(and
.I agent_svid.der
if present) under that directory and runs
.B systemctl \-\-no\-block try-restart spire-agent.service
without waiting for it, so the packaged oneshot, which is ordered before the
agent, finishes first and the next agent start attests the new LDevID. A missing or inactive
.B spire-agent
unit does not fail the renew. The default for
.B \-spire-data
is empty (no cache clear); the packaged oneshot passes the path.
.PP
The packaged oneshot runs after
.B network-online.target
and
.B Before=spire-agent.service
(without
.BR Requires= ).
A daily timer with a one-hour randomized delay repeats the check while the
guest is up. Installing the package enables the timer and the
.B postinst
reloads systemd and starts
.B devid-enroll.timer
(not the oneshot service), so the daily renew is armed without waiting for a
reboot. An immediate boot-time renew still runs via
.B WantedBy=multi-user.target
on the oneshot after the next boot.
Overrides for output and SPIRE data directories may be set in
.IR /etc/default/devid-enroll
(for example
.B DEVID_SPIRE_DATA=/var/lib/spire/agent
on hogan VM 399).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-tpm " path"
TPM device (default
.IR /dev/tpmrm0 ,
the kernel resource manager, which flushes whatever a killed run left loaded;
pass
.I /dev/tpm0
only on a kernel without it).
.TP
.BI \-mds " url"
MDS base URL (default
.IR http://169.254.169.254 ).
.TP
.BI \-out " dir"
Output directory (default
.IR /var/lib/vtpm-mds/devid ).
Run as root, the helper keeps the owner and group of each file it replaces
and gives a new file those of the directory, so a SPIRE agent running as its
own user can read renewed materials. Files that an earlier version left owned
by root keep that owner; hand them to the agent's user once
.RB ( chown )
or move them aside so the next run gives them the directory's owner.
.TP
.BI \-cn " name"
Common Name to put into the platform identity of the signing request.
The service ignores it: the issued certificate's subject is always
.BI CN= vmid
and nothing else.
.TP
.BI \-spire-data " dir"
SPIRE agent
.BR data_dir .
On a PEM change the SVID cache under this directory is cleared and
.B spire-agent
is try-restarted. Empty (the default) disables both. The packaged unit sets
.IR /opt/spire/data/agent .
.TP
.B \-version
Print the package/build version and exit.
.SH SPIRE AGENT CLEANUP
Each renewed LDevID has a new SHA-1 fingerprint, so the SPIFFE agent ID under
.B tpm_devid
changes. Prefer registration selectors
.BI tpm_devid:subject:cn: vmid
over fingerprint paths. After renew, stale server entries can be removed with
SPIRE 1.14
.BR "spire-server agent evict" " (\-spiffeID)"
or
.BR "spire-server agent purge" " (\-expiredFor,"
default
.BR 720h ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vtpm-mds (8),
.BR systemctl (1)
